<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarine</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sarine, in German Saane, is a river of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, about 125 kilometres long and a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aare">Aare</a>. It rises in the Bernese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, flows through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saanen">Saanen</a> and the Gruyère region and past the city of Fribourg, founded on a bend of the river in 1157. Its course roughly follows the language border between French- and German-speaking Switzerland.</p></div>
